1
00:00:46,666 --> 00:00:52,666
Forgive Us Our Trespasses is a drama, war film directed by Ashley Eakin.

2
00:01:33,333 --> 00:01:39,333
Targeted by Nazis as they hunt down and murder people with disabilities, a boy with a
limb difference makes a daring decision while running for his life.

3
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:26,000
Peter, played by Knox Gibson.

4
00:03:06,666 --> 00:03:12,666
Eva, played by Hanneke Talbot.

5
00:03:53,333 --> 00:03:59,333
German officer, played by Justin Mader.

6
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:46,000
Karl, played by Nathaniel McParland.

7
00:05:26,666 --> 00:05:32,666
Older boy, played by Tyler Hutchings.

8
00:06:13,333 --> 00:06:19,333
Young Woman, played by Noah Lamanna.

9
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Forgive Us Our Trespassing is a piece by graffiti artist Banksy
depicting a kneeling boy with a spray-painted halo.

10
00:07:46,666 --> 00:07:52,666
The image can be found on a wall in Salt Lake City, Utah.

11
00:08:33,333 --> 00:08:39,333
In 2010, the image was distributed in the form of posters to
promote the artist's film Exit Through the Gift Shop.

12
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:26,000
In March 2010, an official large-format version of the artwork was displayed at
London Bridge Station in a collaboration between Banksy and Don't Panic.

13
00:10:06,666 --> 00:10:12,666
Transport for London gave permission for this artwork to be hung only if the original image was
altered to remove the yellow dripping spray paint halo, so as to not encourage graffiti.

14
00:10:53,333 --> 00:10:59,333
The print exhibited but removed within 48 hours after the halo was
repaired by "either Banksy or one of his people”.

15
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:46,000
Only one large-format poster of Forgive Us Our
Trespassing now remains in existence.

16
00:12:26,666 --> 00:12:32,666
The film explores themes of neo-nazism, ss (nazi
schutzstaffel), nazi officer, german occupation, disability.

17
00:13:13,333 --> 00:13:19,333
The tone is emotional.
